<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dietrich of Haldensleben</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 985</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dietrich of Haldensleben was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> count who became the first margrave of the Northern March in 965, ruling lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> over the Hevelli and Lutician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>. His harsh rule contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising">Great Slav Rising</a> of 983, in which the Slavs destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havelberg">Havelberg</a> and drove out German rule. He was removed from office soon afterwards and died in 985.</p></div>
